# Yarr *arr

## Gate

Use when the user asks about Sonarr, Radarr (incl. 4K), or Prowlarr
library/search/indexers via yarr MCP. Skip Plex-only, Seerr-only, or
qBit-queue-only asks. Always load `yarr-safety` for writes/deletes.

Never invent series id, movie id, episode id, or indexer id. Resolve via
read actions or ids the user pasted.

## Prefer MCP

When a yarr MCP is ready (`user-mcp_yarr`), use these tools with an
`action` enum:

| Tool | Product |
| --- | --- |
| `sonarr` | TV library / series |
| `radarr` | Movies |
| `radarr_4k` | 4K movie instance |
| `prowlarr` | Indexers / search aggregation |

Shared actions (all four): `service_status`, `api_get`, `api_post`,
`api_put`, `api_delete`, `help`, `codemode`, `op`, `snippet_list`,
`snippet_save`, `snippet_run`, `snippet_delete`.

## Read / search

1. Prefer `service_status` then targeted `api_get` with a path the user
   named or that `help` / prior docs on the tool confirm — do not invent
   undocumented routes.
2. Prefer `op` / snippets only when the user named them or
   `snippet_list` showed them.
3. Paginate with `page` / `page_size` when listing; keep first pulls
   small.
4. Report title + id; never paste API keys from responses.

## Writes

1. `api_post` / `api_put` / `api_delete` and mutating `op` / snippet runs
   need an explicit verb this turn (`yarr-safety`) naming the title or id.
2. Prefer the smallest write (one series/movie) over bulk profile changes.
3. Quality profile / root folder changes are high blast radius — state
   risk, then act only if still authorized.
4. `delete_files` (when the action supports it) is destructive — require
   an explicit verb that covers file deletion, not just library unlink.

## Prowlarr

1. Prefer status + read of indexers before any indexer create/delete.
2. Do not disable all indexers or rotate API keys unless explicitly
   asked.

## Report shape

- Tool (`sonarr` / `radarr` / `radarr_4k` / `prowlarr`)
- Action used
- Title/id (or indexer name) + short finding
- Note when mutate refused for lack of verb

## Out of scope

- Seerr request workflow (see `yarr-seerr`)
- qBit download queue (see `yarr-qbit`)
- Plex library playback (see `yarr-plex`)
- Hard-coded site root folders — resolve from the instance or user

